<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22705" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-dēclīnābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>inflexible</i>, <i>unchangeable</i>, only in a trop. sense (postAug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., of things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virtus animum rectum et indeclinabilem
					praestat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">justitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 74</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">series re rum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 6,
					2</span></i>
			.—Of persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 25, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. 18,
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In gram.: nomen, <i>indeclinable</i>, Diom. pp. 288,
			289 P. — Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indēclīnābĭlĭter</span></b> ,
				adv., <i>unchangeably</i>, Aug. Civ.
			Dei, 9, 22 <i>fin.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
